apple's m1 ipad pro has been out for  over a month and we've already reviewed  both the 11  and 12.9 inch models with the conclusion  that the m1 is the best ipad ever made  in terms of the hardware  but the software is extremely limiting  at least for now  so with that said it's time to look at  everything from a completely different  perspective  because we just got some pretty exciting  leaks and rumors  for the next ipad pro coming in 2022  so the big question we're gonna have to  answer in this video is this  should you wait for the 2022 ipad pro  redesign  or just buy the m1 ipad pro right now  and enjoy it for all of those months  that you would have otherwise ended up  waiting  so without further ado let's get right  into it first up next year's ipad pros  are expected to come in the same exact  11 inch and 12.9 inch sizes  as we currently have which i think makes  sense because the 11 inch  is perfect for portability and the 12.9  inch is right on the verge of being a  bit too large  but the main issue with the current 11  inch model is that it doesn't get the  option for the mini led display  and that's why so many people this year  bought the 12.9 inch ipad pro  including us since we had to review and  test out  that new mini led display but thankfully  we're expecting that new display  to come down to next year's 11 inch ipad  pro model  so that's going to be very exciting for  those who don't want a massive ipad  now moving on to a brand new report from  bloomberg's mark german  who is basically the most reliable apple  leaker out there  the ipad pro is getting a totally new  design next year  with the main difference being a  completely glass back  instead of aluminum just like we have on  the current iphones  and personally i think the glass is  going to look and feel  super premium likely coming with the  same matte texture  that the iphone 12 pro currently has  which i love  and if you're wondering why it's coming  with a glass back that's because apple  is planning to add  wireless charging to the ipad pro which  is going to free up the main thunderbolt  port  so you can use it for connecting  displays storage drives or anything else  and apparently apple is experimenting  with adding reverse  wireless charging to that new ipad pro  at the same time  essentially allowing you to charge your  iphone or earpods  by placing them on the back of the ipad  pro but what makes all of this even more  interesting is that according to mark  german  apple is testing a similar mag safe  charging system  for the ipad pro yes you heard that  right  mac save just like we have on the iphone  12  which is what made me finally start  using wireless charging  especially in the car with this awesome  car mount that i love  and bringing mac safe to the ipad pro  makes perfect sense  because you'll be able to use the same  charging puck for both your iphone  and your ipad making it very convenient  for apple users  on top of that having mac safe on the  ipad is going to enable cool features  like having unique stands that attach  with just  the magsafe system instead of having a  huge plate or  case allowing you to easily rotate the  ipad pro into portrait or landscape mode  but the even bigger deal is that a mac  safe stand will be able to wirelessly  charge the ipad pro  at the same time which is basically the  dream setup  for people who want to use it at home  like people already do with accessories  like the very expensive  kensington studio dock now the only  problem with wireless charging is that  the current version of max safe  isn't very fast at all as you can see in  one of our iphone 12 charging speed  comparisons  where 20 watt max save charging took a  full  hour longer compared to 20 watt wire  charging  but it's even worse for ipads because  they take much longer to charge  due to the larger battery capacities so  apple  will essentially have to upgrade max  safe to make it  faster which is also going to benefit  the iphone now on top of  all of that we're expecting a new magic  keyboard case  to launch alongside the 2022 ipad pros  and that's based on a patent that apple  applied for  showing a new magic keyboard with a  double hinge  which will allow it to sit higher or  fold flat down  onto a table which are things that the  current model can't do at all  and going even further that new magic  keyboard case is going to feature a new  apple pencil holder  within the hinge which will actually  wirelessly charge it  at the same time and if you're wondering  how that's going to be possible  we actually had rumors of a third  generation apple pencil coming  which is going to be shorter than the  current one making it perfect for the  rumored ipad mini 6  and it's going to make it easier to fit  into the new magic keyboards hinge  now in my opinion i think there's a good  chance that apple will build  maxsafe into the magic keyboard itself  to allow for pass-through charging  meaning that  apple will be able to get rid of that  usb-c port built into the current magic  keyboard's hinge  which charges the ipad pro through the  smart connector  which also handles data transfer like  track pad and keyboard  inputs as well as sending ambient light  sensor data  to enable the automatic keyboard  backlighting  the only issue with the smart connector  right now is that the charging speed  using the usb c  port in the hinge is severely limited  compared to charging with the dedicated  thunderbolt port  only accepting 20 watts of power instead  of around 32.6  watts so what apple can do is completely  get rid of the smart connector  altogether  which would make total sense if they're  giving it a glass back  and all of that data and charging would  happen through a  brand new second generation mac safe  wireless charging system  that will also be able to handle data  transfer for all of those keyboard  features  and if you think about it going this  route makes absolutely the most sense  if apple wants to go completely portless  on the iphone  since a new second gen max safe that  handles data transfer  will be required to be able to back up  your iphone  or use recovery software on a mac so the  nice thing about  that new magic keyboard case is that  you'll be able to attach  the max safe charging puck right on the  back of the magic keyboard  so it'll line up perfectly and be able  to pass through charge the ipad pro  allowing you to use the thunderbolt port  for high speed  data transfers and speaking of that new  thunderbolt port the only issue with it  is that it's being limited by the  internal ssds  read and write transfer speeds so  hopefully apple is going to upgrade the  ssds next year  but in terms of performance the 2022  ipad pro  is almost surely getting the future m2  chip  with the same 8 core cpu and 8 core gpu  layout  because the current m1 chip is already  hitting the thermal limits  of the very thin ipad pro's chassis so  in reality the next ipad pro isn't going  to be that much faster than this one  already  is now with all of that said let's go  back and answer the original question  on whether you should be waiting for the  new ipad pro next year  or if you should just buy one right now  and wait for the software to improve  well first of all looking at apple's  timeline for ipad pro releases  there's a good chance that the new model  isn't coming until the fall  of 2022 which is almost a year and a  half from now  basically a very long time to wait on  top of that  the current m1 ipad pro is already close  to being  feature complete or peak ipad if you  think about it it's already got the  thunderbolt port which is the best port  you can get  it's already got the m1 chip which is so  powerful that it's hitting thermal  limits  it's already got a sweet design with the  best stylus the apple pencil  out there it's got face id it's got all  the cameras you would ever need and  lidar  including the new ultra wide selfie  camera  it's got incredible speakers and the  12.9 inch model already has  a killer mini led display so the  question for you is if you think that  new glass back and wireless charging  is going to be worth waiting for as well  as the mini led display coming to the 11  model and the new magic keyboard case  which is likely going to be even more  expensive  especially if you need the new apple  pencil 3  to take advantage of the built-in hinge  charging system as well  as the max safe charging puck that you  need to buy to take advantage of the  wireless charging  so based on all of that i think it would  be wise to just buy the m1 ipad pro  right now  and enjoy it instead of waiting for  something that  might not be that big of an improvement  especially since you're gonna have to  spend a lot of money  for a full setup if you totally disagree  with my thoughts and conclusions go  ahead and comment your thoughts down  below  but if you enjoyed this video definitely  click the circle above to subscribe for  more videos like this one  definitely watch one of those two videos  right there thank you for watching and  we'll see you in the next video
 

